    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d802">

                <pb facs="0748" n="736" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg736"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.24/9–844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Minister to Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-08T14:00:00+03:06">September 8,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>270. I have agreed to joint recommendation that grain shipped under subsidy
                    program for 1944 should be increased from 40,000 tons to 50,000 tons. This
                    represents net increase of 7,000 tons cereal since it includes 3,000 tons grain
                    substituted for dates (re MESC Cairo’s telegram August 26<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d802-f1"/>). In addition to the 50,000 tons is 1,500 tons grain, 300
                    tons sugar and 12 tons tea for the pilgrimage and 3 months’ reserve stocks,
                    arrangements and location of which not yet agreed.</p>
                <p>Agreed also that 50,000 tons grain constitute provisional basis for 1945 supply
                    and shipping purposes to be revised up or down according to developments.
                    Pilgrimage requirements and reverse stock is to be addition to the 50,000
                    tons.</p>
                <pb facs="0749" n="737" xml:id="pg737"/>
                <p>MESC Cairo will cable complete text.<anchor n="50" xml:id="d802-f2"/> Immediate
                    joint instructions on their paragraph 2 needed to end anxiety of Saudi Arabian
                    Government who would be informed urgently.</p>
                <p>Comment follows in separate telegram.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d802-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eddy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
